        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.46,
            0.584,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have noticed that some materials completely disappear when mixed in water. We say that these materials dissolve in water or, in other words, they are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "soluble",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in water (Fig. 6.6a). Some materials do not mix with water and do not disappear even after we stir them for a long time. These materials are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "insoluble",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in water (Fig. 6.6b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.609,
            0.497,
            0.769,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "everything you put in water",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " disappear?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.625,
            0.746,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water plays an important role in the functioning of our body because it can dissolve a large number of materials."
            }
          ]
        },
